
<!--
  PROJECT: Neural Crawler - pom.xml
  ===================================
  This is the Maven Project Object Model (POM) file — the heart of the build system.
  It defines the project metadata, Java version, and all external dependencies this
  application needs to compile and run.

  WHAT IT DOES:
  - Declares the project as a Spring Boot application using the spring-boot-starter-parent,
    which provides sensible defaults for dependency versions, plugin config, and packaging.
  - Pulls in all required libraries: Spring Web (REST layer), Thymeleaf (HTML templating),
    Jsoup (HTML parsing), Apache HttpClient (HTTP requests), Jackson (JSON serialization),
    OpenCSV (CSV export), and the Playwright Java SDK (for JavaScript-rendered pages).
  - Configures the Maven build to produce an executable JAR via the Spring Boot Maven plugin.

  WHY IT EXISTS:
  Without this file Maven cannot resolve dependencies or build the project. Every library
  used across all other files is declared here. Adding or removing a dependency happens
  here first.

  CONNECTS TO:
  - Every Java source file in the project indirectly — they all rely on the libraries
    declared here being on the classpath.
  - The Spring Boot Maven plugin connects to the main application entry point class
    (NeuralCrawlerApplication.java) to package and run the app.
-->
